# Independent shoulder reference — unvalidated draft

Source: OSEL-DAM / U.S. Food and Drug Administration, ShoulderFiniteElementModel,
commit fc9f3e56b104c06759750495be1f8dd5d53c1741.
https://github.com/OSEL-DAM/ShoulderFiniteElementModel/tree/fc9f3e56b104c06759750495be1f8dd5d53c1741

The exact source LICENSE and publisher model notes declare CC0-1.0. The source
LICENSE SHA256 is a2010f343487d3f7618affe54f789f5487602331c0a8d03f49e9a7c547cf0499.
No FDA endorsement, regulatory qualification, medical-device clearance or fitness
for clinical use is implied. Source scientific limitations and disclaimers still
apply; CC0 is not clinical validation. No commercial solver is required here.

Visible Medicine sampled the quadratic tetrahedral boundary at its original
nodes and applied original instance placement. Six parts enter this draft GLB;
source indices remain intact. Vertex normals are interpolated for display only.
No welding, geometry smoothing, decimation, healing, mirroring or per-part fitting
was used. One positive scale plus translation normalizes the source assembly to
unitless display coordinates; positions use float32 with maximum inverse error
3.3131259442598093e-6 unverified source coordinate values, not millimetres.

Humeral cartilage is publisher-constructed, not segmented donor cartilage.
Constructed glenoid cartilage is excluded: two nonmanifold edges and three source
vertices (2798,4501,37871). Connectors are not muscle surfaces and are not loaded.
The publisher reports a right shoulder; anatomical axes, physical units, bone
extent, attachments, intersections and clinical fidelity remain unvalidated.
There is no BodyParts3D or CT/MRI patient-space registration or approval transfer.

This draft has no measurements, anatomical orientation presets or decision
writing. Protected Website Review integration and radiologist sign-off are
separate pending milestones. See docs/FDA_SHOULDER_SOURCE.md for exact input,
conversion, source-node maps, readback and reproduction requirements.
